 "duration": 36.06,
 "lines": "& our younger selves / watching / & dreaming— / While our elders / clutch / their pearls, / hold their faith / & breath closely— ... Life has burned / all my love stories— ... Victory-less / seasons",
 "read": "and our younger selves watching and dreaming, while our elders clutch their pearls, hold their faith and breath closely, freeing their worries peacefully. I've journeyed beyond any place you can conceivably be. So I thought, life has burned all of my love stories. All ends led to losses, victory -less seasons for a man that wanted just one win. I could celebrate forever. Ice has frozen in thought, friendships in death and departure.",
